WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Let's follow the path off Dusty's trail, oh Dusty's trail, Dusty's trail

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
A stage and a wagon ahead and west, part of a wagon train lost from the rest

00:16.000 --> 00:24.000
Dusty's the reason for their flight, thanks to Dusty nothing's right

00:24.000 --> 00:32.000
Only the wagon master's hand keeps them a-rollin' through the promised land

00:32.000 --> 00:37.000
All the goin' gets mighty rough, but they don't seem to mind

00:37.000 --> 00:43.000
It's California, eh, that's the place they must find

00:43.000 --> 00:51.000
Deserts and rocks are in their way, but they won't stop, come what may

00:51.000 --> 00:56.000
Mountains and hills that they must scale, but they know they'll make it

00:56.000 --> 01:01.000
Cause they just can't fail on Dusty's trail

01:11.000 --> 01:15.000
Buddy, is your wagon master around?

01:15.000 --> 01:17.000
He's out watering the horses

01:17.000 --> 01:24.000
Well, we'll wait for him

01:24.000 --> 01:26.000
Oh, that really smells good

01:26.000 --> 01:29.000
Doesn't look too bad, compared to what we'd get in the army

01:29.000 --> 01:33.000
Sure would be nice to sink our teeth into some real grub for a change

01:33.000 --> 01:43.000
Help yourselves

01:43.000 --> 01:55.000
Oh, I forgot to tell you, the potatoes aren't done yet

01:55.000 --> 02:00.000
Cadillac! What are you all buffalo?

02:00.000 --> 02:04.000
Oh, Ryan, what's this? You're still letting me wear those stripes on me

02:04.000 --> 02:08.000
Cookie, you didn't tell me here that your wagon master was an old yellowleg

02:08.000 --> 02:12.000
Yeah, yellowleg, it's a cavalryman that's got a turn of the yellow stripe they wear down their breeches

02:12.000 --> 02:15.000
Ryan here and I used to be in the same company together

02:15.000 --> 02:17.000
Callahan, this is McCorp from here

02:17.000 --> 02:21.000
Sprouse, I want you to meet the best ex-sergeant that ever worked cross sabers

02:21.000 --> 02:23.000
Now you're as full as Barney as ever, aren't you?

02:23.000 --> 02:25.000
Hey, what are you two doing way out here?

02:25.000 --> 02:27.000
We're looking for an army deserter

02:27.000 --> 02:30.000
I've tailed out of the army with the payroll

02:30.000 --> 02:33.000
Have you noticed anyone suspicious around flashing a lot of gold?

02:33.000 --> 02:34.000
No

02:34.000 --> 02:35.000
Dusty, you seen any strangers?

02:35.000 --> 02:36.000
Yeah

02:36.000 --> 02:37.000
Oh, who?

02:37.000 --> 02:40.000
Them

02:40.000 --> 02:45.000
Hey, Dusty, how you coming with dinner?

02:45.000 --> 03:05.000
That's him! He's a deserter!

03:05.000 --> 03:07.000
He's a deserter!

03:07.000 --> 03:14.000
I tell you, that's Webb Matthews, the sidewinder we've been looking for

03:14.000 --> 03:16.000
Will somebody please tell me what's going on here?

03:16.000 --> 03:18.000
He's a member of our wagon train

03:18.000 --> 03:19.000
Well, that cinches it

03:19.000 --> 03:21.000
We heard he joined up with a wagon train

03:21.000 --> 03:23.000
He's the one we're looking for, all right?

03:23.000 --> 03:28.000
Ain't he, Orion?

03:28.000 --> 03:31.000
Mm-hmm, sure

03:31.000 --> 03:33.000
Yes, this is the barman, all right

03:33.000 --> 03:34.000
I'd know him anywhere

03:34.000 --> 03:38.000
I was the courier carrying that payroll, six thousand and gold, and he ambushed me

03:38.000 --> 03:41.000
My head still aches from where he whacked me

03:41.000 --> 03:43.000
Well, maybe the whacking in your head got you all whacked up

03:43.000 --> 03:44.000
I tell you, I'm certain

03:44.000 --> 03:46.000
Will somebody please tell me what's going on?

03:46.000 --> 03:49.000
These men think you're somebody called Webb Matthews

03:49.000 --> 03:53.000
That you're an army deserter and you stole some payroll gold

03:53.000 --> 03:55.000
That's ridiculous

03:55.000 --> 03:58.000
I've been with this wagon train for the past four months

03:58.000 --> 04:01.000
That robbery took place five months ago

04:01.000 --> 04:06.000
Callahan, did you know anything about this man before he joined up with you?

04:06.000 --> 04:07.000
Well, I certainly

04:07.000 --> 04:10.000
And you? You got any proof at all that you're not Webb Matthews?

04:10.000 --> 04:11.000
Well, of course I...

04:11.000 --> 04:15.000
And do you have any proof at all that you didn't hightail it out of the army?

04:15.000 --> 04:17.000
With the company payroll?

04:17.000 --> 04:19.000
No, but that doesn't mean anything

04:19.000 --> 04:22.000
All right, corporal, let's take him back to the camp

04:22.000 --> 04:24.000
Now, wait a minute, Orion Callahan

04:24.000 --> 04:27.000
Now, you know better than to interfere with the army

04:27.000 --> 04:29.000
This whole thing's absurd. I'm not going anywhere

04:29.000 --> 04:31.000
Hold it!

04:31.000 --> 04:34.000
All right, Andy, better go peaceable

04:34.000 --> 04:37.000
It's all right. We know you're innocent

04:37.000 --> 04:41.000
Well, all right, Mr. Callahan, if you say so

04:41.000 --> 04:42.000
All right, let's go

04:47.000 --> 04:50.000
Hey, take it easy on him, Orion

04:50.000 --> 05:05.000
Get this thing straightened out

05:05.000 --> 05:07.000
I know, it's all a misunderstanding

05:07.000 --> 05:10.000
Yeah, they got the wrong guy

05:10.000 --> 05:15.000
Take it from me. I know men

05:15.000 --> 05:18.000
Orion's always been as honest as they come

05:18.000 --> 05:23.000
That's what I can't figure out

05:23.000 --> 05:28.000
Anybody want to eat?

05:28.000 --> 05:29.000
Me either

05:29.000 --> 05:32.000
What do you think about this dreadful situation, Carter dear?

05:32.000 --> 05:36.000
It's quite elementary, really. Andy's innocent

05:36.000 --> 05:38.000
How can you be so certain?

05:38.000 --> 05:43.000
Why would anyone want to steal a paltry $6,000?

05:43.000 --> 05:45.000
What are we going to do about Andy?

05:45.000 --> 05:47.000
Nothing we can do tonight

05:47.000 --> 05:50.000
We can keep on deciding the moment

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
If we can sleep

05:52.000 --> 05:56.000
Mr. Callahan, I'm really worried about Andy

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
So am I

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
I understand

06:00.000 --> 06:04.000
Something about Sprouls and Orion that just doesn't ring true

06:04.000 --> 06:05.000
Yeah

06:05.000 --> 06:06.000
Yeah

06:06.000 --> 06:22.000
Let's go and get some sleep

06:22.000 --> 06:24.000
Hey, what's going on?

06:24.000 --> 06:27.000
We're sure Andy didn't do what those soldiers said

06:27.000 --> 06:33.000
We don't know how yet, but we're going to help him, aren't we Carter?

06:33.000 --> 06:36.000
Non-desertus brookhavenus

06:36.000 --> 06:39.000
A brookhaven never deserts a friend

06:39.000 --> 06:40.000
Damn him off

06:40.000 --> 06:42.000
And we're not leaving Andy behind either

06:42.000 --> 06:44.000
Well of course we're not leaving Andy behind

06:44.000 --> 06:47.000
This wagon train is not going anywhere without him

06:47.000 --> 06:49.000
No wagon master's worth his salt

06:49.000 --> 06:51.000
Don't look after his own

06:51.000 --> 06:55.000
Besides, I got an idea how we can get to the bottom of this whole thing

06:55.000 --> 06:57.000
Mr. Callahan, I could kiss you

06:57.000 --> 07:03.000
Thanks, but right now I need dusting

07:03.000 --> 07:08.000
I ain't going to kiss you

07:08.000 --> 07:10.000
You were saving these old army uniforms for something

07:10.000 --> 07:12.000
Where'd you get all that stuff?

07:12.000 --> 07:13.000
From a cavalry

07:13.000 --> 07:14.000
Yeah

07:14.000 --> 07:18.000
If you take the stripes off of those things, it'll be alright

07:18.000 --> 07:21.000
We're going to put these on and go into that camp

07:21.000 --> 07:24.000
You know that look that Sprouls and Orion gave to each other

07:24.000 --> 07:25.000
Something funny about that

07:25.000 --> 07:26.000
Yeah

07:26.000 --> 07:27.000
And we're doing it for Andy

07:27.000 --> 07:28.000
That's right

07:28.000 --> 07:30.000
I can smell an honest man a mile away

07:30.000 --> 07:31.000
Yeah

07:31.000 --> 07:32.000
Here, here

07:31.000 --> 07:33.000
I like it similar to cavalry

07:38.000 --> 07:41.000
You remember, all you got to do is just blend in with all those soldiers

07:41.000 --> 07:42.000
Okay

07:42.000 --> 07:44.000
And never volunteer for anything

07:44.000 --> 07:45.000
Okay

07:45.000 --> 07:48.000
And keep your mouth shut, I'll do all the talking

07:48.000 --> 07:50.000
Did you hear that?

07:50.000 --> 07:54.000
You keep your mouth shut and I'll do all the talking, alright?

07:54.000 --> 07:56.000
How can I talk with my mouth shut?

07:59.000 --> 08:00.000
Come on

08:04.000 --> 08:05.000
Hey you

08:06.000 --> 08:07.000
Us?

08:07.000 --> 08:08.000
Where are you two going?

08:11.000 --> 08:15.000
Well, I'll tell you, we was going to go down there and have a swim

08:15.000 --> 08:16.000
You got a pass?

08:16.000 --> 08:17.000
No

08:17.000 --> 08:18.000
You?

08:18.000 --> 08:19.000
He's doing the talking

08:19.000 --> 08:20.000
Huh?

08:20.000 --> 08:23.000
Yeah, well he can't talk so he's got a sore throat

08:23.000 --> 08:27.000
Suppose the both of you just go back in camp and I'll forget you were sneaking out

08:27.000 --> 08:28.000
Alright, alright

08:33.000 --> 08:35.000
Well, so far so good

08:37.000 --> 08:41.000
Don't salute anybody unless they got some gold on their shoulders, huh buddy?

08:44.000 --> 08:45.000
Hey

08:45.000 --> 08:49.000
Look, look, look, look, look

08:49.000 --> 08:52.000
Boy, I bet he didn't bring us to dinner first

08:57.000 --> 08:58.000
Let's go

09:01.000 --> 09:02.000
Hey, Andy

09:02.000 --> 09:03.000
What's up?

09:03.000 --> 09:04.000
Yeah, what's up?

09:04.000 --> 09:06.000
I'm asking, what are you doing here in those uniforms?

09:06.000 --> 09:08.000
We come to get you out of here, we know you're innocent

09:08.000 --> 09:10.000
Mr. Gallagher ain't gonna smell you a mile away

09:10.000 --> 09:12.000
You know, if you're telling the truth then Spalzer's lying

09:12.000 --> 09:14.000
Don't you worry about a thing, Andy, we're gonna find all the facts

09:14.000 --> 09:15.000
It's too loud

09:17.000 --> 09:19.000
I appreciate what you're doing but you're taking your life in your hands

09:19.000 --> 09:20.000
Also a mustache

09:21.000 --> 09:22.000
What's happening?

09:22.000 --> 09:26.000
Uh, we were just having a look around sir

09:26.000 --> 09:29.000
Well talking to prisoners isn't allowed, don't you have other duties?

09:29.000 --> 09:31.000
No sir, we don't volunteer for anything

09:31.000 --> 09:35.000
Oh, well I'm volunteering you for that drill squad over there, get moving

09:35.000 --> 09:36.000
Yes sir

09:38.000 --> 09:39.000
Gold, gold

09:39.000 --> 09:44.000
Gold, gold, gold

09:53.000 --> 09:56.000
Uh, here, here you two, hit, snap to it

09:56.000 --> 09:59.000
Now you two fall in with the rest of them recruits

09:59.000 --> 10:01.000
Now let's look alive in here now, squad

10:01.000 --> 10:04.000
Right, right, and hut

10:05.000 --> 10:06.000
Left, hey

10:06.000 --> 10:08.000
Forward, hut

10:08.000 --> 10:09.000
One, hut

10:09.000 --> 10:11.000
Two, three, hut

10:11.000 --> 10:12.000
One, hut

10:12.000 --> 10:14.000
Three, hey

10:14.000 --> 10:16.000
Forward, hut

10:16.000 --> 10:17.000
Two, three, hut

10:17.000 --> 10:18.000
One, hut

10:18.000 --> 10:20.000
Hit, hit, hit

10:20.000 --> 10:21.000
What's going on back here?

10:21.000 --> 10:24.000
Fire, fire, fire

10:24.000 --> 10:25.000
Right, right, fire

10:25.000 --> 10:27.000
Right, right, right

10:27.000 --> 10:28.000
Right, right, right

10:28.000 --> 10:30.000
Hit, hit, hit

10:30.000 --> 10:31.000
One, hut

10:31.000 --> 10:33.000
Two, three, hut

10:33.000 --> 10:35.000
Two, three, hut

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
Oh shut up, what are you doing in that drill?

10:38.000 --> 10:39.000
Turn it up, turn it up

10:39.000 --> 10:40.000
Let it be long now

10:40.000 --> 10:44.000
So court-martial that wagon train guy and webbing me will be off the hook

10:44.000 --> 10:45.000
I don't like it

10:45.000 --> 10:47.000
I just don't like it

10:47.000 --> 10:49.000
You don't have to like it Orion

10:49.000 --> 10:52.000
You just go along with it and you'll get your share of the gold

10:52.000 --> 10:54.000
Enough to pay off your gambling debts

10:54.000 --> 10:57.000
Either that or a bullet in your gut, take your pick

10:57.000 --> 11:00.000
That Orion never could play poker

11:00.000 --> 11:04.000
As soon as I identify that guy at the trial, I'm off to join Webb

11:04.000 --> 11:07.000
We'll split up the loot and send you what's coming to you

11:07.000 --> 11:09.000
Hey, the three of them are in this thing together

11:09.000 --> 11:13.000
Yeah, it was a sorry day when I met the likes of you

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
We all have our price Orion

11:15.000 --> 11:18.000
All I did was meet yours

11:18.000 --> 11:27.000
Hey come on, we gotta go save Andy

11:27.000 --> 11:31.000
Hold it right there

11:31.000 --> 11:33.000
Callie

11:33.000 --> 11:35.000
You're under arrest

11:42.000 --> 11:44.000
Well I don't mind telling you people, I'm worried

11:44.000 --> 11:47.000
Now Callahan and Dusty should have been back by now

11:47.000 --> 11:49.000
I hope nothing's happened to them

11:49.000 --> 11:51.000
I'll go, so will I

11:51.000 --> 11:54.000
No, no, no, no, it's my place, I won't hear a tale of it

11:54.000 --> 11:57.000
Besides, it is a man's job

11:57.000 --> 12:02.000
No offense Mr. Brookhaven, but I really think Lulu and I could do a better job

12:02.000 --> 12:05.000
But what do you mean?

12:05.000 --> 12:12.000
Well you see there are things that we could accomplish with soldiers that you can't

12:12.000 --> 12:18.000
Oh no, of course, that is a possibility I hadn't thought of

12:18.000 --> 12:23.000
So what can they do? We're not in the army anyway, so they'll make us civilians

12:23.000 --> 12:28.000
Listen, we are charged with spying and impersonating soldiers Dusty, we're in big trouble

12:28.000 --> 12:31.000
Hey, okay

12:31.000 --> 12:46.000
Let's break it up, huh?

12:46.000 --> 12:50.000
Wait, what?

12:50.000 --> 12:58.000
Dusty, in a second

12:58.000 --> 13:07.000
No, no, here

13:07.000 --> 13:09.000
Wait, I'm getting good

13:09.000 --> 13:11.000
Let's try it again, huh?

13:11.000 --> 13:17.000
Put the lock down

13:17.000 --> 13:19.000
Oh here I know, I think I got it

13:19.000 --> 13:28.000
Mandy

13:28.000 --> 13:57.000
Mandy

13:57.000 --> 14:01.000
Just a minute ladies, state your business please

14:01.000 --> 14:05.000
Oh, well you see our wagon train was passing through the territory

14:05.000 --> 14:08.000
And we heard there was a little old army encampment nearby

14:08.000 --> 14:13.000
Are you what they call a major or a colonel?

14:13.000 --> 14:21.000
Well, no, not exactly, my job's more important

14:21.000 --> 14:25.000
Oh Betsy, did you hear that? That's so exciting

14:25.000 --> 14:31.000
What do you do? I keep those outside from coming in and those inside from going out

14:31.000 --> 14:38.000
It does sound important, but why would anyone want to leave a delightful place like this?

14:38.000 --> 14:45.000
Three prisoners like to give it a try

14:45.000 --> 14:49.000
Prisoners? Yep, awaiting court, Marsha

14:49.000 --> 14:52.000
General Cunningham's coming tomorrow to preside over the trial

14:52.000 --> 14:56.000
That sounds so thrilling, what do you suppose is going to happen to them?

14:56.000 --> 15:00.000
What do you think happens to spies and deserters?

15:00.000 --> 15:07.000
Oh my, we'd give anything if we could see a real live prisoner

15:07.000 --> 15:09.000
Anything?

15:09.000 --> 15:28.000
I'll see what I can do

15:28.000 --> 15:32.000
This here Cunningham's coming in tomorrow to run the whole shebang

15:32.000 --> 15:33.000
You're wrong, Lulu

15:33.000 --> 15:35.000
But that's what the sentry said

15:35.000 --> 15:50.000
I'll see them in a day, here's what I want you to do

15:50.000 --> 16:00.000
Private, you will please inform your commanding officer that General Cunningham has arrived to preside over the court martial

16:00.000 --> 16:06.000
My stagecoach broke down two miles down the road and my men are repairing it

16:06.000 --> 16:08.000
But the general wasn't expected until tomorrow

16:08.000 --> 16:10.000
Tomorrow what? Tomorrow, sir

16:10.000 --> 16:12.000
Tomorrow what? Sir General Cunningham, sir

16:12.000 --> 16:15.000
That's better, I'm recommending you for corporal

16:15.000 --> 16:20.000
Now hurry up and announce me to your commanding officer, I have to get back to the war

16:20.000 --> 16:21.000
What war is that, sir?

16:21.000 --> 16:24.000
Sentry, there is always a war going on somewhere

16:24.000 --> 16:48.000
Yes sir, right just way sir

16:48.000 --> 16:53.000
These are great seats, right down front

16:53.000 --> 16:58.000
Team, come

16:58.000 --> 17:01.000
General Cunningham, sir, how good to see you

17:01.000 --> 17:04.000
Oh, have you met me before?

17:04.000 --> 17:06.000
Oh I know sir

17:06.000 --> 17:08.000
Oh then, this is indeed a pleasure sir

17:08.000 --> 17:13.000
May I introduce my wife, Mrs. General Cunningham

17:13.000 --> 17:17.000
And my two lovely daughters, Miss Lulu Bell Cunningham

17:17.000 --> 17:20.000
And Miss Betsy Bell Cunningham

17:20.000 --> 17:34.000
Charming, ladies will you be seated

17:34.000 --> 17:41.000
We can begin the trial sir

17:41.000 --> 17:43.000
Where's my gavel?

17:43.000 --> 17:47.000
Right here sir

17:47.000 --> 17:50.000
Plain oak, I'm accustomed to mahogany

17:50.000 --> 17:53.000
Oh well, I suppose you have to make doom out here in the wilderness

17:53.000 --> 17:57.000
I hope it never gets back to the point

17:57.000 --> 18:01.000
Well, who is the trial counsel here?

18:01.000 --> 18:04.000
I am sir

18:04.000 --> 18:05.000
I am sir

18:05.000 --> 18:09.000
You are? You're kind of young, you sure you know your law?

18:09.000 --> 18:11.000
I studied at Yale sir

18:11.000 --> 18:14.000
Yale?

18:14.000 --> 18:17.000
It's not exactly Harvard, is it?

18:17.000 --> 18:21.000
But I suppose some of us have to struggle through life with some sort of a handicap

18:21.000 --> 18:26.000
Alright, gentlemen, you may call your first witness

18:26.000 --> 18:31.000
The court calls Corporal Sprouls

18:31.000 --> 18:35.000
Can you identify the man who attacked you and stole the army payroll?

18:35.000 --> 18:37.000
Yes sir, it was Webb Matthews

18:37.000 --> 18:41.000
Is he present? And if so, can you point him out?

18:41.000 --> 18:46.000
That's him

18:46.000 --> 18:48.000
I object

18:48.000 --> 18:51.000
Sir, you can't object, you're the presiding officer

18:51.000 --> 18:56.000
A mere technicality, are you familiar with the case of Lucas versus White?

18:56.000 --> 18:57.000
No sir

18:57.000 --> 19:01.000
Well, the objection is sustained, are you going to get back to your law books?

19:01.000 --> 19:04.000
Yes sir

19:04.000 --> 19:08.000
The court now calls Sergeant Orion as a witness

19:08.000 --> 19:10.000
Yes sir

19:10.000 --> 19:15.000
Sergeant, will you tell the court what the other two prisoners were doing when you apprehended them?

19:15.000 --> 19:20.000
Yes sir, well you see they were in uniform pretending to be soldiers

19:20.000 --> 19:23.000
And they were spying on this here military outpost

19:23.000 --> 19:26.000
Orion, you're a disgrace to that uniform

19:26.000 --> 19:27.000
I object

19:27.000 --> 19:34.000
Your objection is completely out of line, Lieutenant, are you familiar with the case of Wayne versus Garrett?

19:34.000 --> 19:35.000
Yes sir

19:35.000 --> 19:37.000
You are?

19:37.000 --> 19:44.000
Well there's this other case of Duval versus Lovelace, that reverses Wayne versus Garrett

19:44.000 --> 19:49.000
No sir, the Tyson-Danbury decision reversed Wayne versus Garrett

19:49.000 --> 19:53.000
Correct

19:53.000 --> 19:58.000
I'm just putting you to the test and you passed for once

19:58.000 --> 20:04.000
Sir, I don't believe I need more testimony, and I'm prepared to deliver my summation

20:04.000 --> 20:13.000
Well, I hope it's a brief one, in the immortal words of Chief Justice John Marshall, a brief summation is a good summation

20:13.000 --> 20:15.000
Never

20:15.000 --> 20:24.000
In all the annals of military history, have any more dastardly crimes been committed by a soldier and his two cohorts?

20:24.000 --> 20:30.000
To assault a poor, defenseless, enlisted man in the act of doing his duty?

20:30.000 --> 20:37.000
To steal the hard earned wages of our self-sacrificing brave fighting men?

20:37.000 --> 20:47.000
To dress up in an honorable uniform for the dishonorable purpose of ferreting out military secrets and delivering them to the enemies of the United States of America

20:47.000 --> 20:51.000
The home of the free and the land of the brave

20:51.000 --> 20:55.000
Sir, is nothing short of treason

20:55.000 --> 21:00.000
I'm not guilty of treason

21:00.000 --> 21:07.000
Well, uh

21:07.000 --> 21:12.000
Well done Lieutenant, I was carried away with your eloquence

21:12.000 --> 21:21.000
Now we must hear from the defense side, who is the defense counsel here?

21:21.000 --> 21:24.000
I will speak with the three of us sir

21:24.000 --> 21:30.000
I agree with everything the lieutenant says about that robbery, the only trouble is he's got the wrong man

21:30.000 --> 21:35.000
